========================================================================================
LRC-14 ANGLE 4: SELBERG-BEURLING NONNEGATIVE MINORANT (dual of Bedert Riesz). stdlib only.
worst core S = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 98]    true L ~ 0.005223
========================================================================================

[1] THE IMPOSSIBILITY THEOREM (headline)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A nonneg trig poly m with m<=1_safe must satisfy m<=0 on the CLOSED danger band [-1/14,1/14]
and m>=0 there too, hence m=0 on a full interval => m=0 identically (real-analyticity).
So the ONLY valid nonneg POINTWISE minorant of 1_safe at any finite degree is m=0 (bound 0).
Bedert's Riesz product is the exact DUAL and hits the mirror wall: the indicator's sharp
edge blocks BOTH extremal-function routes.

[2] CONCRETE nonneg trig poly: Fejer bump c*F_M(theta-1/2), c=1/(M+1)  (provably 0<=m<=1)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     M   c0=int m  leak into danger  sup_danger m  (c0 must DROP toward 0)
     7    0.12500          0.001284      0.016253
    14    0.06667          0.000345      0.004646
    21    0.04545          0.000157      0.002164
    28    0.03448          0.000089      0.001247
    40    0.02439          0.000042      0.000609
   -> c0=int m = 1/(M+1) DECREASES; a sharper bump spreads mass, never approaches 6/7.

[3] GRID-LP minorant numbers (scipy reference, GRID ARTIFACTS of the impossibility)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A grid LP enforcing m<=0 only at finitely many danger grid points reports growing c0,
   but those m are NOT true nonneg pointwise minorants (they poke >0 between grid points).
   Reference (scipy.optimize.linprog, grid N=24000):
      K=7 : c0~0.345 ; K=14 : c0~0.564 ; K=21 : c0~0.669 ; K=28 : c0~0.718
   Their TRUE product integral (computed exactly + grid cross-check) collapses to ~0:
      int prod m  ~ 1.1e-24 (K7), 3.5e-18 (K14), 2.7e-13 (K21), 4.2e-12 (K28)
   i.e. ~15 orders below L~0.005223. POSITIVE in sign (beats Riesz's 1.0096>=1) but USELESS.

[4] EXACT product constant term for the PROVABLY-VALID Fejer bump (true certificate value)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     M        c0       c0^13   EXACT int prod m    grid check     /L_true
     7   0.12500   1.819e-12          1.633e-15     1.633e-15    3.13e-13
    14   0.06667   5.138e-16          6.775e-18     6.776e-18    1.30e-15
    21   0.04545   3.536e-18          7.783e-23     7.784e-23    1.49e-20
   (EXACT lattice value and direct grid integral AGREE: the bound is genuinely ~1e-15..1e-23.
    Note: the bump is a minorant of the constant 1, not of 1_safe, so this is an UPPER proxy;
    a true 1_safe-minorant would be even smaller. Either way: no useful positive bound.)

[5] VERDICT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 DEAD-END for inf L>0.  The extremal-MINORANT route Bedert avoided fails for a clean reason:
 the impossibility theorem (no nonzero nonneg trig poly minorizes an indicator on a closed
 band) caps the only valid finite-degree certificate at 0, and any grid-relaxed surrogate
 collapses under the (.)^13 product to ~1e-15.  The transferable nugget is the theorem in [1].
 The genuine remaining direction is NOT a 1-D extremal function but a POSITIVITY/SOS
 certificate on the 12-dim relation lattice of the product trig poly (moment-SDP), which
 abandons the per-runner Selberg framework entirely.

DONE.
